{
  "name": "ISAAC location confidence recalibration maps",
  "applies_to": "location_prob (and contender_location_prob) in ISAAC labeled_location files",
  "input": "the raw score as released, in [0, 1]",
  "output": "estimated probability that the location label is correct",
  "method": "isotonic regression, fitted on the validation split of held-out authors and evaluated on the test split; monotone and non-parametric, so it preserves the ordering of the raw scores while correcting their scale",
  "how_to_apply": "pick the map matching the row's tier, then linearly interpolate the score into (x, y) with clipping at both ends: numpy.interp(score, x, y). Tier follows from the label: two-letter code -> state, EUROPE/AMERICAS/ASIA_OCEANIA/AFRICA -> region, US/NON_US -> top, UNK -> no score.",
  "choosing_a_condition": "use 'masked' unless you know the authors state their location explicitly; it is the conservative map and the closer analogue for corpus authors who never self-disclose. 'standard' applies to authors who do. At the state tier the two disagree by up to .35 in accuracy at the same score.",
  "limitations": "calibration holds in aggregate on the population the map was fitted on (authors whose location was recoverable from explicit self-disclosure). Per-state and per-subgroup calibration were not assessed.",
